{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cg15UfEhgzdLv29RcCitC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HMfKwBYfHX491maXho46eS","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q019_stable_periodic_release_semantics","answer":"The current-release endpoint (/api/v1/releases/current) reports SCOPe version 2.08 as the current release. Its stable label is \"2.08-stable\" (freeze date 2021-07-28, release date 2021-09-22, db_name SCOPe, is_public true, is_comprehensive false). The latest periodic update reported is version \"2.08-2026-08-16\", dated 2026-08-16.\n\nWhich identifier to cite: for a reproducible analysis you should cite the stable release identifier, SCOPe 2.08 (\"2.08-stable\"), because the stable release is a frozen snapshot: its classification hierarchy (class/fold/superfamily/family sunids and sccs identifiers), domain definitions, and the ASTRAL sequence and PDB-style domain files do not change after the freeze. If your work actually used entries that only exist in the periodic update (e.g., newly auto-classified PDB entries), cite the exact dated periodic label \"2.08-2026-08-16\" so a reader can retrieve that specific snapshot; citing just \"2.08\" or \"latest\" would be ambiguous because the periodic content keeps growing over time.\n\nWhat the periodic label means: SCOPe periodic updates (labelled <stable version>-<YYYY-MM-DD>) are incremental additions layered on top of a stable release. They add new PDB entries classified automatically into existing families/superfamilies (plus some manual curation) without changing the stable release's existing hierarchy or domain boundaries; new nodes/folds are generally reserved for the next stable release. They are published on a rolling basis (the release list shows e.g. 2.07 with periodic update 2.07-2021-07-07 before 2.08 froze on 2021-07-28), so a periodic label identifies a dated, superseding snapshot of the 2.08 line rather than a new numbered release. Limits: the periodic update is not a comprehensive re-classification (is_comprehensive is false for all SCOPe 2.x releases), automated periodic assignments rely on sequence similarity to already-classified domains and are therefore less thoroughly curated than stable-release manual assignments, and a periodic snapshot may later be superseded by a newer dated update or by the next stable release (e.g., 2.09), so analyses depending on the newest entries should record the full dated label.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08","/api/v1/releases"]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2553,"cache_read_input_tokens":9920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2553},"output_tokens":75,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4237ec1c-01a2-4a77-ba37-8c9ae1c114cf","uuid":"a5e2ec17-60f0-4829-aed6-5aebfe8a6f33","timestamp":"2026-10-13T23:08:48.293Z","request_id":"req_011Cg15Uf1Zn3LfkSwrZ6p95","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HMfKwBYfHX491maXho46eS":{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q019_stable_periodic_release_semantics","answer":"The current-release endpoint (/api/v1/releases/current) reports SCOPe version 2.08 as the current release. Its stable label is \"2.08-stable\" (freeze date 2021-07-28, release date 2021-09-22, db_name SCOPe, is_public true, is_comprehensive false). The latest periodic update reported is version \"2.08-2026-08-16\", dated 2026-08-16.\n\nWhich identifier to cite: for a reproducible analysis you should cite the stable release identifier, SCOPe 2.08 (\"2.08-stable\"), because the stable release is a frozen snapshot: its classification hierarchy (class/fold/superfamily/family sunids and sccs identifiers), domain definiti